    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0048" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)Colombia/651: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-04-10T22:00:00-05:00">April 10, 1943—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 11—2:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>649. Department’s telegram 375, March 24, 4 p.m.; and 443, April 7.<anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d39-f1"/> In today’s courier pouch, completed draft of proposed air
                    rubber agreement just received, is being forwarded by Mayer<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d39-f2"/> to Rubber Development Corporation for attention Bicknell.
                    Mayer and La Spina occur [<hi rendition="#italic">concur?</hi>] in recognition
                    of cooperation of Colombian officials for expediting conclusion of this
                    agreement, and as it conforms in major respects with draft memorandum of
                    agreement which was transmitted with Department’s instruction No. 763 of
                    November 10, 1942,<anchor n="68" xml:id="d39-f3"/> that it should be signed here
                    as promptly as possible after text arrives and has been examined in Washington.
                    Contrary to Department’s apparent understanding no exchange of diplomatic notes
                    on the air rubber agreement has been effected. As this agreement is one case of
                    implementation of the over-all strategic materials agreement already covered by
                    and [<hi rendition="#italic">an</hi>] exchange of notes no additional diplomatic
                    exchange will be necessary. Signatures of Mayer and the Ministry of War will
                    suffice. Since it is impossible for Embassy to make copies of agreement in time
                    for this pouch it is hoped that copy sent to Rubber Development Corporation will
                    meet Department’s needs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lake</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
